Package: cayleyR
Type: Package
Title: Cayley Graph Analysis for Permutation Puzzles
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R: c(
    person(
      "Yuri", "Baramykov",
      email = "lbsbmsu@mail.ru",
      role = c("aut", "cre"),
      comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0000-7627-4217")
    )
  )
Description: Implements algorithms for analyzing Cayley graphs of
    permutation puzzles. Provides methods for cycle detection, state space
    exploration and finding optimal operation sequences, for the TopSpin
    puzzle, whose group is generated by shift and reverse operations, and
    for Rubik's cubes of any size, whose moves are generated from the
    geometry as a turn of one layer about one axis, so that the slice
    turns of the 3x3x3 and the inner layers of larger cubes follow from
    the same rule as the face turns. The 3x3x3 is solved by four human
    methods --- CFOP, layer by layer, and the blindfolded Old Pochmann
    and M2 --- and by a two-phase search after Herbert Kociemba
    <https://kociemba.org/cube.htm>, following the implementation in
    'twips' <https://github.com/cubing/twips>, which reaches the same
    cube in a fraction of the moves. Also provides rule-defined landmark
    states for probing
    graphs too large to enumerate, and convex and non-convex hulls for
    measuring the solid such states span. The method Iterative Cycle
    Intersection (ICI) is described in Yuri Baramykov (2026)
    <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2607.13219>.
